development.question_text:
Sketch $y=(x-1)^{2}(x+3)$, showing the intercepts and the behaviour at each root.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4.4,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
1. **Determine the end behaviour from the leading term.**
Leading term is $x^{3}$, so as $x\to\infty$, $y\to\infty$.
2. **Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$.**
$y=(-1)^{2}(3)=3$
3. **Find the $x$-intercepts by letting $y=0$.**
$x=1,\ -3$
4. **State the behaviour at each $x$-intercept and draw the curve.**
Bounce at $x=1$ (double root); cut at $x=-3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4.4,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.49:2.36,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.30*(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x+3)});
\fill (-3,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (-3,0) {$(-3,0)$};
\fill (1,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (1,0) {$(1,0)$};
\fill (0,0.9) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (0,0.9) {$(0,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

