mastery.question_text:
Sketch $y=x^{4}-8x^{3}+16x^{2}$ by factorising first. Show the intercepts and the behaviour at each root.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2,0)--(5.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
$y=x^{4}-8x^{3}+16x^{2}$
$=x^{2}(x^{2}-8x+16)$
$=x^{2}(x-4)^{2}$
1. **Determine the end behaviour from the leading term.**
Leading term is $x^{4}$, so as $x\to\infty$, $y\to\infty$ (even degree — both ends up).
2. **Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$.**
$y=0$
3. **Find the $x$-intercepts by letting $y=0$.**
$x=0,\ 4$
4. **State the behaviour at each $x$-intercept and draw the curve.**
Bounce at $x=0$ and at $x=4$ (both double roots) — the curve never goes below the axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2,0)--(5.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.08:5.07,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.10*\x*\x*(\x-4)*(\x-4)});
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$(0,0)$};
\fill (4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$(4,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
